<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Newham on Rowan Amateur Radio Society</title><link>https://www.rowanars.net/tags/newham/</link><description>Recent content in Newham on Rowan Amateur Radio Society</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rowanars.net/tags/newham/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Rowan ARS Field Day 2026 – Photos</title><link>https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/</link><pubDate>Sat, 27 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Between Friday 6/26 and wrapping up on Sunday 6/28/26, under Mark K&amp;rsquo;s leadership, we had a fantastic field day. We made contacts, we grew friendships, and grew stronger in unity as a club. Needless to say, we&amp;rsquo;re looking forward to the &lt;a href="https://www.rowanars.net/events/field-day-2027/"&gt;2027 Field Day event&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The Salisbury Post wrote a feature article and visited the event:&#10;&lt;a href="https://www.salisburypost.com/2026/06/30/ham-it-up-rowan-radio-society-joins-natl-event/"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ham it up: Rowan radio society joins nat’l event&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; by Janet Briggs&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="stations" id=stations&gt;&#10; Stations&#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;a UHF/VHF station brought by Ralph&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;an HF station brought by Aaron&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;SSB Phone&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;2 HF stations brought by Mark&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;1 FT8/&lt;em&gt;WSJT-X&lt;/em&gt; digital station&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;1 CW station&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;a club HF station for &lt;strong&gt;G&lt;/strong&gt;et &lt;strong&gt;O&lt;/strong&gt;n &lt;strong&gt;T&lt;/strong&gt;he &lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;ir&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;!--&#10;## Antennas&#10;For base stations, we used at least two end-fed half-wave antennas, several varieties of vertical antennas.&#10;--&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="event-photos" id=event-photos&gt;&#10; Event Photos&#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="photo-gallery"&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9083.jpg" class="gallery-item"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9083_hu_7c512e03622c173b.jpg" alt="IMG_9083.jpg" loading="lazy"&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9085.jpg" class="gallery-item"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9085_hu_9d605b4f634a449b.jpg" alt="IMG_9085.jpg" loading="lazy"&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9086.jpg" class="gallery-item"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9086_hu_9784922881498c30.jpg" alt="IMG_9086.jpg" loading="lazy"&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9087.jpg" class="gallery-item"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9087_hu_a23505b90fea9128.jpg" alt="IMG_9087.jpg" loading="lazy"&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9088.jpg" class="gallery-item"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9088_hu_5e1069febd08449f.jpg" alt="IMG_9088.jpg" loading="lazy"&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;a href="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9089.jpg" class="gallery-item"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://www.rowanars.net/posts/2026-rowanars-fieldday/IMG_9089_hu_ca85c13